# Mercedes Simplex 60 hp, 1903-1909.
#
# The great pre-1914 Mercedes: about 4,389 mm long, 1,700 mm wide, 2,300 mm high,
# 2,950 mm wheelbase (body-dependent); 9,236 cc four, about 60 hp, chain drive,
# good for roughly 110 km/h. A photographed substitute for the unverifiable
# "Napier 60 hp" entry in the section F table. The height is the closed
# Reiselimousine body as photographed, not the much lower open tourer; the earlier
# 1,650 mm figure was an estimate for an open body and is wrong for this one.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mercedes_Simplex
#
# Colours: White, Dark Green, Maroon and Black are documented period finishes.
#
# Weight: 10 in total (white 4, green 3, maroon 2, black 1).
#
# Speed 110 km/h; comfort 55/413 (line). Class 4.
# Dates: 1903-1909 with a road tail to about 1932.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/mercedes-simplex-60.blend. References:
# citycars/references/mercedes-simplex-60/ (gitignored). Images via Wikimedia
# Commons.

obj=citycar
